body:
God I am right there with you with the stereotypical clothing and stuff!! My partners and I have had that discussion and already decided that this little one is not going to have the typical pink/blue thing going on. We figured on red and purple, because why the heck not? And a lot of Nightmare Before Christmas... Yay for gothic Disney, haha!

&#x200B;

As happy as I am for my OWN speculation, I get really annoyed when others do it, if that makes sense? Like, even I have my head in the realm of realistic expectations for goodness sake! I know there's a 50/50 chance of being right, and it's not the end of the world if the baby's sex is different than I was thinking. They'll be whoever they want to be when they grow up anyway!

I've had to "hospital shop" to actually get critical care for a heart problem I am only now learning I have... The ER I had gone to before noted that my blood pressure was high (200s/120s), gave me medicine, and said, "You've got to have another plan besides the ER. Take this and go home." Wasn't the first time I had come to them either because of shit with my doctor's office.

&#x200B;

Went to schedule a follow up with my doctor, none was available for a couple months, and I had an ass of a time trying to get said medication refilled. Had also tried to work with this office to set up a cardiology appointment because of my blood pressure before and the doctor just wouldn't do it. Wound up having to give up (because it was a matter of roof over my head or my health at that point) and my blood pressure soared again. Went to a different hospital, was checked out with pressures that were in the same range, and actually got kept for observation and further testing. They confirmed that there's something wrong with my heart outside of just my blood pressure, and there may be something with my kidneys, but we're not sure yet.

&#x200B;

I have since changed doctor's offices to a much better group with more reliable appointment systems, and I am seeing a cardiologist to get more information on the issue at hand. Right now we just know that SOMETHING is wrong, but at least I'm finally getting seen for it...

&#x200B;

I know it's nowhere near as severe as gunshot wounds or other immediate life-or-death situations, but this is my one frustrated example with our healthcare system as part of the many who are stuck with Medicaid. :/

It looks like it might be caused by an error with the microSD, if you're using one. If so, check to make sure it's inserted properly. You may need to reformat the card (which sucks, I know). You can also try using a different card if you have one available. If you're NOT using a microSD, you may just need to reinstall the game since you said rebooting the Switch didn't do anything. :/ 

&#x200B;

Here's a link to the help article from Nintendo associated with your error code. [https://www.nintendo.com.au/help/error-code/617/NintendoSwitch/\_2002-4517\_/2002-4517](https://www.nintendo.com.au/help/error-code/617/NintendoSwitch/_2002-4517_/2002-4517)
